            "bug_id": 19356,
            "text": "Created attachment 4138\npatch: no copy for DATAPTR_OR_NULL() on a wrapper's shared data (on top of attachment 4136)\n\nHere is a second, small patch, on top of attachment 4136. Since r90261 the wrapper's `Dataptr_or_null` method duplicates shared data so that it can return a pointer. For example, with `x <- runif(1e6)` and `y <- structure(x, a = 1)`, `sum(y)` copies the data of `x`. R 4.6.1 did not.\n\nWith the patch the method returns NULL while the data is shared and not yet locked, and callers read through `Get_region`. No pointer is handed out, so the guarantee from r90309 is unaffected, and `DATAPTR_OR_NULL()`, which is not called with the GC disabled, no longer allocates. `sum()`, `mean()`, `max()`, `anyNA()` and `is.unsorted()` stop copying; `REAL_RO()` still does, as it has to return a pointer. Regression test included; `make check` passes on macOS arm64.\n\nBoth patches are in https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/521.",
